Changes in v5:
- also refuse a large send whose IP length is not the frame length:
  bytes past the IP length stay in a bridged or switched frame, so
  gso_segs computed from the IP length undercounted the segments the
  egress path produces (Sashiko review of v4)
- KUnit: a large send with payload and bytes past the IP length is
  refused, its GSO fields and TCP checksum field left alone
- KUnit: header-only IPv4 and IPv6 frames with a matching IP length
  are refused, so a case still fails without the TCP payload check
- message and helper comment: a refused frame is left unchanged and not
  trusted, rather than "checked by the stack", which bridged or
  switched frames are not
- wrap three lines over 80 columns

New in v4: the helper header checks from v3 patch 4, split out with
their own Fixes: tags.
